208 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Gut health refers to how well your digestive system breaks down food, absorbs nutrients, and supports the lining of the intestines. It also reflects how the gut works with the immune system, metabolism, and nervous system. When this system works well, it supports comfort, regularity, and overall resilience.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

209 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(At the center of gut health is the microbiome, a community of bacteria and other microorganisms that live mainly in the large intestine. These microbes support digestion, help protect the gut barrier, and influence immune and inflammation balance. A healthy gut is about keeping this internal environment balanced and resilient.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

